# VEDA tool mirror configuration
#
# Copy this file to  installer/mirror.conf  and set MIRROR to where you
# uploaded the bundle produced by ./veda-pack. Once it is committed, every
# later install is just:  ./install.sh
#
# Override at any time with:  ./install.sh --mirror <url>
#                             VEDA_MIRROR=<url> ./install.sh
# Disable with:               ./install.sh --no-mirror
#
# The installer verifies every download against installer/manifest/mirror.manifest,
# so this file holds no secrets and is safe to commit.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RECOMMENDED: GitHub Release assets on a PRIVATE repository
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2 GiB per asset, assets live outside git history, CDN-backed and resumable,
# versioned by tag, and a private repo keeps the DTU-licensed tools behind
# your own access control. Collaborators run `gh auth login` once.
#
#   ./veda-pack --upload gh://your-org/veda-tools@tools-v1
#
MIRROR=gh://your-org/veda-tools@tools-v1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Alternatives
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Any web server, S3, Cloudflare R2, Backblaze B2, institutional space.
# Each tool is fetched from <base>/<filename>. Simplest and most predictable.
# MIRROR=https://files.your-lab.example/veda/tools-v1/

# Google Drive, via gdown. Works, but every VEDA archive is over Drive's
# ~25 MB virus-scan threshold, and Drive applies frequency-based quota
# lockouts (HTTP 403/429, up to ~24h) that will bite when several people
# install on the same day. Not recommended for shared use.
# MIRROR=gdrive://1AbCdEfGhIjKlMnOpQrStUvWxYz

# Any rclone remote. Goes through the provider's real API, so it avoids
# Drive's interstitial and public-link quota completely. The best way to
# actually use Drive/OneDrive/Dropbox. Needs `rclone config` once.
# MIRROR=rclone://gdrive:veda/tools-v1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Licence reminder
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NetMHCpan, NetMHCIIpan, GibbsCluster, Seq2Logo and DeepLoc are licensed by
# DTU Health Tech for your own academic use and may NOT be redistributed.
# If your bundle includes them, the mirror must be access-controlled. Use
# ./veda-pack --free-only to build a bundle that is safe to host publicly.
